\name{og_simulation_design}
\alias{og_simulation_design}
\title{Simulation designs of the paper}
\description{
Settings of Experiments A, B and C of the paper: the process, the design sampler, the error variance and the regression function, ready for \code{\link{og_simulate}}.
}
\usage{
og_simulation_design(experiment = c("A", "B", "C"), design = c("A", "B"),
        prob2 = 0.5, scenario = c("interaction", "usual"), delta = 0.45,
        sign = 1)
}
\arguments{
  \item{experiment}{\code{"A"}, \code{"B"} or \code{"C"}.}
  \item{design}{design of Experiment A.}
  \item{prob2}{probability of a second measurement in Experiment B.}
  \item{scenario}{regression of Experiment C, see \code{\link{og_scenario}}.}
  \item{delta}{amplitude of the interaction.}
  \item{sign}{sign of the interaction in Experiments A and B.}
}
\details{
Experiment A uses the rotating process \eqn{X(t) = Z_1\cos(2\pi t) + Z_2\sin(2\pi t)}{X(t) = Z_1 cos(2 pi t) + Z_2 sin(2 pi t)}, one noiseless measurement and the interaction regression. Under design A the time is uniform on \eqn{\{0, 1/4\}}{{0, 1/4}} and the interaction is invisible; under design B it is uniform on \eqn{[0,1]}{[0, 1]} and the interaction is identified, although both designs carry the same linear information.

Experiment B uses Brownian motion with two orthonormal contrasts supported on \eqn{[0,1/2]}{[0, 1/2]} and \eqn{[1/2,1]}{[1/2, 1]}, one or two measurements per subject with probability \code{prob2} of a second one, and error variance 0.05. The interaction of the contrasts is identified only through subjects measured twice.

Experiment C uses a rank-four process with Fourier eigenfunctions and eigenvalues 1, 0.6, 0.35 and 0.2, between one and four measurements with probabilities 0.4, 0.3, 0.2 and 0.1, error variance 0.1, and the regression of \code{\link{og_scenario}}. Experiment D is generated by \code{\link{og_simulate_bm}}.
}
\value{
A list with \code{process}, \code{design}, \code{sigma2}, \code{g} and \code{r}.
}
\examples{
\dontrun{
set.seed(1)
## Experiment A: the interaction is invisible under design A and estimable under design B
for (d in c("A", "B")) {
  des <- og_simulation_design("A", design = d)
  dat <- og_simulate(2000, des$process, des$design, des$sigma2, des$g, des$r)
  fit <- og_fit(dat, dat$Y, des$process, des$sigma2, Q = 2, design = des$design)
  print(round(fit$orders[[2]]$theta, 3))   # V1*V2: 0 under design A, near 0.166 under design B
}
## settings of Experiments B and C
desB <- og_simulation_design("B", prob2 = 0.5)
desC <- og_simulation_design("C", scenario = "usual")
}
}
